To extract data from an Excel table in Java, you can use the Apache POI library. Here is an example of Java code that reads data from an Excel table and determines the major elements of comedy:
```java
import java.io.FileInputStream;
import java.io.IOException;
import org.apache.poi.ss.usermodel.Cell;
import org.apache.poi.ss.usermodel.Row;
import org.apache.poi.ss.usermodel.Sheet;
import org.apache.poi.xssf.usermodel.XSSFWorkbook;
public class ComedyElementsExtractor {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        try {
            FileInputStream file = new FileInputStream("comedy.xlsx");
            XSSFWorkbook workbook = new XSSFWorkbook(file);
            Sheet sheet = workbook.getSheetAt(0);
            int rowCount = sheet.getLastRowNum();
            int element1Count = 0;
            int element2Count = 0;
            int element3Count = 0;
            int element4Count = 0;
            for (int i = 1; i <= rowCount; i++) {
                Row row = sheet.getRow(i);
                Cell cell = row.getCell(1);
                String element = cell.getStringCellValue();
                if (element.equals("Slapstick")) {
                    element1Count++;
                } else if (element.equals("Irony")) {
                    element2Count++;
                } else if (element.equals("Satire")) {
                    element3Count++;
                } else if (element.equals("Parody")) {
                    element4Count++;
                }
            }
            System.out.println("Major elements of comedy:");
            System.out.println("Slapstick - " + element1Count + " examples");
            System.out.println("Irony - " + element2Count + " examples");
            System.out.println("Satire - " + element3Count + " examples");
            System.out.println("Parody - " + element4Count + " examples");
            file.close();
        } catch (IOException e) {
            e.printStackTrace();
        }
    }
}
```
Assuming the Excel table has two columns, with the first column containing the name of a sitcom or movie and the second column containing the major element of comedy used in that sitcom or movie, the code reads the data from the Excel table and counts the number of examples of each major element of comedy. The results are then printed to the console.
Note that you will need to download and add the Apache POI library to your project in order to use it in your code.

