├── Bacteria
├── Archaea
└── Eukarya
    ├── Plants
    ├── Fungi
    └── Animals
        ├── Invertebrates
        └── Vertebrates
            ├── Fish
            ├── Amphibians
            ├── Reptiles
            ├── Birds
            └── Mammals
```
This cladogram illustrates the evolutionary relationships among living organisms. It shows that all living organisms can be grouped into three domains: Bacteria, Archaea, and Eukarya. The Eukarya domain is further divided into four kingdoms: Plants, Fungi, Animals, and Protists. The Animals kingdom is divided into two groups: Invertebrates and Vertebrates. The Vertebrates group is further divided into five classes: Fish, Amphibians, Reptiles, Birds, and Mammals.
