Here's a Java code that utilizes recursion to search for the artifact in the maze:
```
public class Maze {
    private int[] rooms;
    private int artifactRoom;
    public Maze(int[] rooms, int artifactRoom) {
        this.rooms = rooms;
        this.artifactRoom = artifactRoom;
    }
    public int search(int startRoom) {
        if (startRoom == artifactRoom) {
            return startRoom;
        } else {
            int leftRoom = -1;
            int rightRoom = -1;
            // Search the left room
            if (startRoom - 1 >= 0 && startRoom - 1 < rooms.length) {
                leftRoom = search(startRoom - 1);
            }
            // Search the right room
            if (startRoom + 1 >= 0 && startRoom + 1 < rooms.length) {
                rightRoom = search(startRoom + 1);
            }
            // Determine which room to search next based on the binary search algorithm
            if (leftRoom != -1 && leftRoom == artifactRoom) {
                return leftRoom;
            } else if (rightRoom != -1 && rightRoom == artifactRoom) {
                return rightRoom;
            } else if (leftRoom != -1 && rooms[leftRoom] < rooms[startRoom]) {
                return leftRoom;
            } else if (rightRoom != -1 && rooms[rightRoom] < rooms[startRoom]) {
                return rightRoom;
            } else {
                return -1;
            }
        }
    }
}
```
To use this code, you would create an instance of the `Maze` class with the array of room numbers and the number of the room containing the artifact. Then you would call the `search` method with the number of the starting room. The `search` method would recursively search through the maze until it finds the artifact room, and then return the number of that room.
Note that this code assumes that the array of room numbers is sorted in ascending order. If the array is not sorted, you would need to modify the binary search algorithm accordingly. Additionally, this code does not handle cases where there are multiple artifacts in the maze.

