To analyze online product reviews and identify potential biases in Java, we can use Natural Language Processing (NLP) techniques and algorithms. Here are some steps to follow:
1. Data Collection: First, we need to collect data from online product reviews. We can use web scraping techniques to extract review data from popular e-commerce websites like Amazon, eBay, etc.
2. Data Pre-processing: Once we have collected the data, we need to preprocess it to remove any unwanted characters, punctuation marks, and stop words. We can also perform stemming and lemmatization to reduce the words to their root form.
3. Sentiment Analysis: After preprocessing, we can perform sentiment analysis on the reviews to determine whether they are positive, negative or neutral. We can use libraries like Stanford CoreNLP or Apache OpenNLP for this purpose.
4. Biases Detection: Next, we need to detect any biases in the reviews. We can use techniques like Latent Dirichlet Allocation (LDA) or Principal Component Analysis (PCA) to identify topics that are frequently mentioned in the reviews. We can also use algorithms like K-means clustering to group similar reviews together.
5. Mitigation: Finally, we can mitigate the impact of biases on the review ratings by using techniques like sentiment weighting or topic weighting. We can assign weights to the reviews based on their sentiment or topic and then calculate the overall rating.
Here is some sample code that demonstrates the above process:
```
// Data Collection
String url = "https://www.amazon.com/product-reviews/12345";
Document doc = Jsoup.connect(url).get();
Elements reviews = doc.select("div.review");
// Data Pre-processing
for (Element review : reviews) {
   String text = review.select("span.review-text").text();
   text = text.replaceAll("[^a-zA-Z0-9\\s]", "").toLowerCase();
   String[] words = text.split("\\s+");
   List<String> filteredWords = new ArrayList<>();
   for (String word : words) {
      if (!StopWords.isStopWord(word)) {
         filteredWords.add(Stemmer.stem(word));
      }
   }
   String filteredText = String.join(" ", filteredWords);
   review.attr("filtered-text", filteredText);
}
// Sentiment Analysis
for (Element review : reviews) {
   String filteredText = review.attr("filtered-text");
   int sentimentScore = SentimentAnalyzer.getSentimentScore(filteredText);
   review.attr("sentiment-score", sentimentScore);
}
// Biases Detection
List<String> topics = TopicModeling.getTopics(reviews);
for (Element review : reviews) {
   String filteredText = review.attr("filtered-text");
   double topicScore = TopicModeling.getTopicScore(filteredText, topics);
   review.attr("topic-score", topicScore);
}
// Mitigation
double sentimentWeight = 0.5;
double topicWeight = 0.5;
double overallRating = 0.0;
for (Element review : reviews) {
   int sentimentScore = Integer.parseInt(review.attr("sentiment-score"));
   double topicScore = Double.parseDouble(review.attr("topic-score"));
   double weight = sentimentWeight * sentimentScore + topicWeight * topicScore;
   overallRating += weight;
}
overallRating /= reviews.size();
System.out.println("Overall Rating: " + overallRating);
```
Note that the above code is just a sample and may need to be modified according to your specific requirements.

