To integrate XML data into the platform, we can use programming languages such as Java, Python, or PHP to read and write XML files. For example, the following Java code snippet shows how to read a course syllabus from an XML file:
```
import java.io.File;
import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilder;
import javax.xml.parsers.DocumentBuilderFactory;
import org.w3c.dom.Document;
import org.w3c.dom.NodeList;
import org.w3c.dom.Node;
public class CourseReader {
  public static void main(String[] args) {
    try {
      File inputFile = new File("course.xml");
      DocumentBuilderFactory dbFactory = DocumentBuilderFactory.newInstance();
      DocumentBuilder dBuilder = dbFactory.newDocumentBuilder();
      Document doc = dBuilder.parse(inputFile);
      doc.getDocumentElement().normalize();
      System.out.println("Course title: " + doc.getElementsByTagName("title").item(0).getTextContent());
      System.out.println("Instructor: " + doc.getElementsByTagName("instructor").item(0).getTextContent());
      System.out.println("Description: " + doc.getElementsByTagName("description").item(0).getTextContent());
      System.out.println("Topics:");
      NodeList topics = doc.getElementsByTagName("topic");
      for (int i = 0; i < topics.getLength(); i++) {
        Node topic = topics.item(i);
        System.out.println(topic.getTextContent());
      }
    } catch (Exception e) {
      e.printStackTrace();
    }
  }
}
```
This code reads the course information from an XML file called "course.xml" and prints it to the console. Similarly, we can use XML parsing libraries in other programming languages to read and write XML data in the virtual reality-based global educational network.

